{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5wppxbh6gv4haeeuphjfnaa72eksaeyxybewdgpwfz4fnp6i45ta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Summary of what I found and did:\n\n## The project\n`c_src/src/main.c` is a 41-line executable: it reads one `double` with `scanf(\"%lf\", &f)` (leaving `f` at `0.0f` on failure) and prints `\"%llx %a %.4f\\n\"`. Byte-identical output therefore requires emulating glibc's `%lf` token scanner, `strtod` (decimal **and** hex), and `%llx`/`%a`/`%.4f` formatting.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all derived mechanically from the C)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly `driver` + `main`. I restructured the crate (`src/imp.rs` logic, `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle]` wrappers + `crate-type=[\"cdylib\",\"rlib\"]`, `src/main.rs` thin entry) so the Rust `.so` exports **the same two names**. `nm -D` diff is empty in both directions; 0 non-libc undefined symbols. 1 of 1 C file, 2 of 2 C functions translated — nothing was skipped, nothing stubbed.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — the C has *zero* explicit error paths, so the whole rejection surface is `scanf`'s matching/input failures: **24 rows**, one per distinct `conv_error`/`no-conversion` branch.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — **36 rows** over the axes the C actually branches on. `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and CMake has no options, so there is one feature combination; I enumerate it mechanically in `run_diff_tests.sh` and also cover the `[profile.release]` (`panic=\"abort\"`) build.\n\n## Phases B–D — differential testing\nFive `harness = false` suites (sequential, because comparison redirects process-wide fd 0/1) `dlopen` **both** `.so`s and call only `driver`/`main`, plus process-level runs of both executables:\n\n**132 075** `.so` comparisons + **889** process-pair comparisons + 1 092 error-path comparisons — all byte-identical, across **default / `--no-default-features` / `--release`**.\n\n## Bugs found (in my harness, not the C)\n- libtest's progress output leaked into fd-1 captures → switched to `harness = false`.\n- glibc's `fseek` can satisfy a rewind from the **stale stdio read buffer**, feeding the previous test's input to `scanf` → the C side now `freopen`s per input.\n\n## Negative controls (proving the tests bite)\nInjecting `\"0x\"→\"0X\"` in `%a` fails every `driver` row; dropping the sign term from the bare-hex-prefix rejection (`-0x` → `-0.0`) fails `errors::row_19`. Notably a flat byte fuzzer **missed** that second bug — only the ERRORS.md-derived row and a token-grammar generator caught it, which is exactly why Phase C is derived from the C's branches rather than from fuzzing.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (only the sanctioned `build/` output). Run everything with `./run_diff_tests.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":271967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":441,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2690a3f-cb75-437d-9bda-108d7d432746","uuid":"63e30c55-51a3-4e63-bf4a-1647e61e54f9","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:15:16.239Z"}
